   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/DesignCompromises.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "en": "Increases the base range of all non-beam Energy and Hybrid weapons by %s.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/EnergyBoltCoherer.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "en": "Originally designed by the Tri-Tachyon Corporation for use on its combat droneships, the coherence field strength has to be dialed down to allow operation on crewed vessels.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/EnergyBoltCoherer.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "en": "Since the base range is increased, this range modifier - unlike most other flat modifiers in the game - is increased by percentage modifiers from other hullmods and skills.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/EnergyBoltCoherer.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "en": "The coherence field is unstable under combat conditions, with stresses on the hull resulting in spot failures that release bursts of lethal radiation. Crew casualties in combat are increased by %s.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/EnergyBoltCoherer.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "en": " telemetry quality",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/EscortPackage.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "en": "Can not be installed on capital ships",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/EscortPackage.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "en": "Can not be installed on frigates",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/EscortPackage.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "en": "Escort package",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/EscortPackage.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "en": "no connection",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/EscortPackage.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "en": "Ship does not have standard fighter bays",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/ExpandedDeckCrew.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "en": "Faulty Automated Systems",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/FaultyAutomatedSystems.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "en": "Ship does not suffer from CR degradation",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/FragileSubsystems.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "en": "A ship with high resolution sensors increases the fleet's sensor range by %s/%s/%s/%s, depending on hull size. Each additional ship with high resolution sensors provides diminishing returns. The higher the highest sensor range increase from a single ship in the fleet, the later diminishing returns kick in.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/HighResSensors.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "en": "Ships with high resolution sensors",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/HighResSensors.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "en": "The total sensor strength increase for your fleet is %s.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/HighResSensors.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "en": "This ship's combat readiness is below %s and its high resolution sensors can not be utilized. Bringing this ship into readiness would increase the fleetwide bonus to %s.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/HighResSensors.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "en": "Beam weapons deal %s more damage and deal hard flux damage to shields.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/HighScatterAmp.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "en": "Incompatible with Advanced Optics",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/HighScatterAmp.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "en": "Reduces the portion of the range of beam weapons that is above %s units by %s. The base range is affected.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/HighScatterAmp.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 31,
   "en": "The base range is reduced, thus percentage and multiplicative modifiers - such as from Integrated Targeting Unit, skills, or similar sources - apply to the reduced base value.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/HighScatterAmp.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 32,
   "en": "Increased Maintenance",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/IncreasedMaintenance.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 33,
   "en": "Can only be installed on civilian-grade hulls",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MilitarizedSubsystems.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 34,
   "en": " CAPACITY REMAINING",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 35,
   "en": "A combat-rated autoloader that provides a limited number of reloads, out of a shared reload capacity, to missile weapons installed in small missile mounts.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 36,
   "en": "A partial reload is possible when running out of capacity.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 37,
   "en": "Affected weapon",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 38,
   "en": "After a reload, the weapon requires an extra %s seconds, in addition to its normal cooldown, before it can fire again.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 39,
   "en": "CAPACITY EXHAUSTED",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 40,
   "en": "Determined by ship size and number of small missile slots, both filled and empty. Having fewer of these simplifies the task and increases the number of possible reloads.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 41,
   "en": "Does not affect weapons that do not use ammo or regenerate it, or are mounted in any other type of slot. Reload size is not affected by skills or hullmods that increase missile ammo capacity.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 42,
   "en": "No affected weapons mounted",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 43,
   "en": "Reload capacity",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 44,
   "en": "Reload cost",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 45,
   "en": "Ship does not have any small missile slots",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 46,
   "en": "Small missiles",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 47,
   "en": "missile weapons installed in small missile mounts",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/MissileAutoloader.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 48,
   "en": "Can not be installed on this ship",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/NeuralIntegrator.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 49,
   "en": "Can only be installed on automated ships, install Neural Interface instead",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/NeuralIntegrator.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 50,
   "en": "After the transfer is complete, the target ship's system cooldown (if any) will be reset, and if the ship system uses charges, it will gain an additonal charge. This effect operates on a cooldown equal to %s the cooldown/charge regeneration time saved by it.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/NeuralInterface.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 51,
   "en": "Can not be installed on automated ships, install Neural Integrator instead",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/NeuralInterface.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 52,
   "en": "Neural system reset",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/NeuralInterface.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 53,
   "en": "Requires the Neural Link skill to function",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/NeuralInterface.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 54,
   "en": "Use the \"",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/NeuralInterface.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 55,
   "en": "benefit from your combat skills",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/NeuralInterface.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 56,
   "en": "Can not remove while ship has point-defense weapons installed",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PDIntegration.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 57,
   "en": "Emergency dive!",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseAnchor$PhaseAnchorScript.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 58,
   "en": "Emergency phase dive",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseAnchor$PhaseAnchorScript.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 59,
   "en": "Incompatible with Adaptive Phase Coils",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseAnchor.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 60,
   "en": "zero",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseAnchor.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 61,
   "en": "Fleetwide sensor strength increases - such as from High Resolution Sensors - do not factor into this calculation.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseField.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 62,
   "en": "In addition, the fleet's detected-at range is reduced by a multiplier based on the total sensor profile of the %s highest-profile ships in the fleet, and the total sensor strength of the %s phase ships with the highest sensor strength values. This effect only applies when the fleet's transponder is turned off.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseField.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 63,
   "en": "Phase ships in fleet",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseField.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 64,
   "en": "Removing this ship would change the multiplier to %s. Adding another ship with the same sensor strength would improve it to %s.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseField.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 65,
   "en": "The detected-at range multiplier for your fleet is %s. The fleet's transponder must be off for the multiplier to be applied.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseField.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 66,
   "en": "The sensor profile of the %s top ships in your fleet is %s. The sensor strength of the top %s phase ships is %s.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseField.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 67,
   "en": "This ship's combat readiness is below %s and the phase field's fleetwide effect can not be utilized. Bringing this ship into readiness would improve the multiplier to %s.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseField.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 68,
   "en": "transponder must be off",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/PhaseField.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 69,
   "en": "Can not be installed on automated ships",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/RecoveryShuttles.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 70,
   "en": "Incompatible with Makeshift Shield Generator",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/ShieldShunt.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 71,
   "en": "Ship has no shields",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/impl/hullmods/ShieldShunt.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 72,
   "en": "Allow black market purchases",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 73,
   "en": "Always add \"Blast Doors\"",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 74,
   "en": "Always add \"Reinforced Bulkheads\"",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 75,
   "en": "Buy ordnance from market",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 76,
   "en": "Buy weapons and fighter LPCs from market, if docked at one.\n\nOrdnance from your cargo will be preferred if that option is checked and if the alternatives are of equal quality.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 77,
   "en": "Buy weapons and fighter LPCs from the black market.\n\nNon-black-market options will be preferred if the alternatives are of equal quality.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 78,
   "en": "Makes the loadout only loosely based on the goal variant.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 79,
   "en": "Prioritizes installing the \"Blast Doors\" hullmod, which increases hull integrity and greatly reduces crew losses suffered due to hull damage.\n\n\"Blast Doors\" may still be added if this option isn't checked, provided there are enough ordnance points.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 80,
   "en": "Prioritizes installing the \"Reinforced Bulkheads\" hullmod, which increases hull integrity and makes a ship virtually certain to be recoverable if lost in battle.\n\n\"Reinforced Bulkheads\" may still be added if this option isn't checked, provided there are enough ordnance points.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 81,
   "en": "Randomize weapons and hullmods",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 82,
   "en": "Remove everything possible prior to autofitting; generally results in a better fit.\n\nHowever, refitting outside of port reduces a ship's combat readiness, and this option tends to lead to more changes and more readiness lost.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 83,
   "en": "Spend any unused ordnance points on flux vents, capacitors, and essential hullmods.\n\nWill not make any changes to weapon loadout, will not affect ship modules (if any), and will not spend any credits.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 84,
   "en": "Spend free OP",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 85,
   "en": "Strip before autofitting",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 86,
   "en": "Upgrade weapons using extra OP",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 87,
   "en": "Use ordnance from cargo",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 88,
   "en": "Use ordnance from storage",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 89,
   "en": "Use weapons and fighter LPCs from your fleet's cargo holds.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 90,
   "en": "Use weapons and fighter LPCs from your local storage facilities.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
  },
  {
   "i": 91,
   "en": "Use weapons better than the ones specified in the goal variant, if there are ordnance points left to mount them.\n\nWill add flux vents and capacitors up to the number specified in the goal variant first, then upgrade weapons, and then add more vents and some common hullmods.\n\nLeaving some unspent ordnance points in a goal variant can help take advantage of this option.",
   "ctx": "starfarer.api.jar:com/fs/starfarer/api/plugins/impl/CoreAutofitPlugin.class"
